TinQa Procurement Backend - local commands
==========================================

LOCAL DATABASE: scripts/dev/db.sh (the same file is in TinQa_Ecommerce_BE; settings in scripts/dev/db.conf)

    scripts/dev/db.sh                         after any backend or database change (keeps your data)

  It checks that Postgres is running (localhost:5432/tinqa_procurement), backs up the DB to
  backups/tinqa_procurement_<date>.dump (the newest 10 are kept), stops if an applied migration was edited, lists
  the new migrations and asks before running one that removes data, migrates (each migration in its own
  transaction), then runs mvn clean spring-boot:run. Redis must be running too.

    scripts/dev/db.sh status                  applied and pending migrations
    scripts/dev/db.sh backup                  backup only
    scripts/dev/db.sh restore backups/<file>  put a backup back (backs up the current data first)
    scripts/dev/db.sh repair                  after a failed migration was fixed, or an applied one was edited on
                                              purpose and the database already has its result
    scripts/dev/db.sh reset                   drop every table and migrate an empty DB (deletes ALL data)

  Options: --yes skips the questions, --no-backup skips the backup, --no-start migrates without starting the app.
  DB_HOST / DB_PORT / DB_NAME / DB_USER / DB_PASSWORD override the settings. Flyway runs through the pom's
  flyway-maven-plugin, which uses the same Flyway version as the app.

WRITING A SCHEMA CHANGE SO DATA IS KEPT
  Add a new file src/main/resources/db/migration/V{next}__what_changed.sql. Never edit a migration that has
  already run. Then change the entity to match (ddl-auto: validate stops the app if they differ).

    New column            ALTER TABLE t ADD COLUMN c TEXT;                         -> existing rows get NULL
    New column, empty     ALTER TABLE t ADD COLUMN c TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '';     -> existing rows get ''
    New required column   ADD COLUMN as NULL; UPDATE t SET c = ...; ALTER TABLE t ALTER COLUMN c SET NOT NULL;
    Renamed column        ALTER TABLE t RENAME COLUMN old_name TO new_name;        -> values kept
    Renamed table         ALTER TABLE old_t RENAME TO new_t;                       -> rows kept
    Removed column        ALTER TABLE t DROP COLUMN c;                             -> that column's values removed

  Do not write a rename as a DROP plus an ADD, because that loses the values. The script warns when a new
  migration does both.

OTHER COMMANDS
  run application only:  mvn spring-boot:run
  clean compile:         mvn clean compile
  DB clean (deletes the data in every table except employee, employee_address, users and flyway_schema_history):
                         psql -h localhost -U tinqa_app -d tinqa_procurement -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -f scripts/dev/reset_dev_data.sql
